<title>SINGAPORE: Ampol to shut 23,000-bpd FCC Feb 21 for 2-3 weeks.</title>
<headline>Ampol to shut 23,000-bpd FCC Feb 21 for 2-3 weeks.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Petroleum Pty Ltd (Ampol) will shut down its 23,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) fluid catalytic cracker (FCC) at 115,000-bpd Kurnell refinery on February 21 for two to three weeks as scheduled, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said the planned shutdown will not cause any product shortfall for the company.</p>
<p>Ampol is jointly owned by Pioneer International Ltd and Caltex Australia Ltd.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
